,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":47,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-16T11:47:47.162902","tool_call_id":"call_awx3pOBR4djZXLwGKOWFbeEt","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":47,"usage":null},{"content":"I see that my phone is connected to a cellular network, but the signal is poor and it’s only on 2G. Also, it looks like data roaming is actually off, even though you mentioned it was enabled. Could this be causing the slow or unreliable internet? What should I do next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":48,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-16T11:47:48.453724","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":48,"usage":{"completion_tokens":63,"prompt_tokens":2818}},{"content":"Yes, the poor signal and connection to only 2G network can definitely cause slow and unreliable mobile data. Also, if data roaming is off on your phone, you won't be able to use mobile data properly while in France even if roaming is enabled on your line.\n\nTo improve your mobile data speed and reliability, please do the following on your phone:\n1. Turn ON data roaming on your phone.\n2. Change your network mode preference to \"4G/5G preferred\" to allow your phone to connect to faster networks.\n\nI can guide you through these steps or perform the network mode change remotely if you want. Would you like me to proceed with changing the network mode preference first?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":49,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-16T11:47:50.957323","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":49,"usage":{"completion_tokens":141,"prompt_tokens":9275}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":50,"thinking